# hugmesh-tor-reconcile — Tor v3 onion-service refresh timer (24h default).
#
# The TIMER half of the onion-service reconcile (the OpenRC oneshot runs the agent
# once at boot; this cron entry re-runs it daily). cronie reads /etc/cron.d (the same
# mechanism the egress-VPN + backup + device-registry-sync timers use). Installed ONLY
# when the 'tor' optional service is selected (PR gate).
#
# The agent is FAIL-SOFT + idempotent: the v3 onion keypair is minted once on first
# boot and PERSISTS (off-git, tor:tor) so the .onion address is stable; the daily run
# just re-asserts the managed torrc + re-exports the hostname (and would re-mint only
# if the keypair were ever lost). Initial mint is at boot, not here.
#
# Field order: min hour dom month dow user command
0 0 * * * root /usr/sbin/hugmesh-tor-reconcile >> /var/log/hugmesh-tor-reconcile.log 2>&1
